From: VAP scale optimization series
Subject: [PATCH 0012] cel: drop AstToCheckedExpr discard, intern ReturnTypes() slices

Two related per-CompileCELExpression wastes in the
admission/plugin/cel pipeline.

1. compile.go:348-352 called cel.AstToCheckedExpr(ast) and discarded
   the result, only checking the error. The single error case is
   `!ast.IsChecked()`, which is unreachable here because env.Compile
   on the line above returned no issues. The comment at line 350 even
   admits "should be impossible since env.Compile returned no issues".

   ToProto walks the entire AST building a *exprpb.CheckedExpr proto
   tree (refMap + typeMap + recursive ExprToProto over every node),
   then everything is discarded. Per-call cost scales with AST node
   count:

      trivial expression `true`                  857 B / 12 allocs
      simple   `"a" == "b"`                    1 480 B / 24 allocs
      realistic 3-clause &&                    5 720 B / 88 allocs
      complex  containers.all(c, ... 6 conds) 17 216 B / 252 allocs

   Removed.

2. Every ExpressionAccessor.ReturnTypes() implementation in the tree
   was `return []*celgo.Type{X}`, a fresh slice literal allocated on
   every call. ReturnTypes is invoked twice per CompileCELExpression
   (once for the cache key, once inside compileFresh). Replaced each
   with a package-level singleton variable initialised once. Affected:

      pkg/admission/plugin/policy/validating/interface.go:
          ValidationCondition, AuditAnnotationCondition, Variable
      pkg/admission/plugin/policy/validating/message.go:
          MessageExpressionCondition
      pkg/admission/plugin/policy/validating/typechecking.go:
          celExpression
      pkg/admission/plugin/policy/mutating/plugin.go:
          Variable
      pkg/admission/plugin/policy/mutating/patch/json_patch.go:
          JSONPatchCondition
      pkg/admission/plugin/policy/mutating/patch/smd.go:
          ApplyConfigurationCondition
      pkg/admission/plugin/webhook/matchconditions/matcher.go:
          MatchCondition

   Each return-types slot saved ~13 ns / 8 B / 1 alloc per call:
      BenchmarkReturnTypes_FreshSliceLiteral-8   13.5 ns/op   8 B/op   1 allocs/op
      BenchmarkReturnTypes_PackageSingleton-8     1.0 ns/op   0 B/op   0 allocs/op

End-to-end CompileCELExpression bench (compileFresh end-to-end with
real environment), before vs after both fixes:

                     before bytes/op   after bytes/op   delta
   trivial            10 322 B          9 466 B         -856 B   (-8%)
   simple             15 912 B         14 430 B       -1 482 B   (-9%)
   realistic          60 713 B         54 980 B       -5 733 B   (-9%)
   complex           178 182 B        160 932 B      -17 250 B  (-10%)

                     before allocs    after allocs     delta
   trivial            199              187             -12
   simple             313              289             -24
   realistic        1 155            1 067             -88
   complex          3 050            2 798            -252

At 5000 policies × 5 expressions of moderate complexity per refresh
that's ~450 MB of transient compile-time allocation eliminated per
full-refresh tick, plus a bunch of dead defensive code that never
caught a real error.

Includes compile_waste_bench_test.go which isolates each waste site
and provides regression coverage.

Tested:
  go test ./staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/admission/plugin/cel/...           PASS
  go test ./staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/admission/plugin/policy/...        PASS
  go test ./staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/admission/plugin/webhook/...       PASS
  go test ./staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/cel/...                            PASS

